  "narrative": {
    "status": "ok",
    "headline": "Collin County Power Backup Report",
    "summary": "Homes in Collin County face an elevated risk of long power outages. Records from the past 8 years since 2018 show a long outage about once every 10 years. In February 2021, 34% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth faced about 73 hours for outages of 12 hours or longer. In May 2024, 23% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth faced about 51 hours for outages of 12 hours or longer. One Core lasts about 16 hours in January. One Core lasts about 35 hours in November. Two Cores last about 32 hours in January. Base confirms sizing at install.",
